{
 "schema_version": "ROW_ENTRIES_RECEIPT_V1",
 "rule_id": "entry-gate-rule-v1-a-row-of-another-entry-than-the-words-is-withheld-and-a-row-of-its-own-entry-stands-whatever-its-points",
 "what": "a row with a line in the corpus lane's row entries ledger carries, in the facts slot (slot 10, an object), n: the Strong's numbers of the entries its own source files it under, where it has any; t: for a row of a source whose entries are STEP's own tags, those that carry STEP's letter; b: for a row of a source that names BDB's own entries, those entries. A row whose same-source twin under a key ending in a maqaf was struck carries, after its own, the entries of that twin's line that it lacked (followed.entries_given_to_a_twin names each pair). The texts are the served bytes, unchanged. At a place the gate reads these against the tag of the word's core piece. A row of a further source named by a list of the pin (lists) carries n as its line gives it: the numbers of the Bible dictionaries' entries its own pointed head form and kind of word meet, joined by the corpus lane",
